<title>USA: Weeks Corp Q3 net shr rises to $0.27.</title>
<headline>Weeks Corp Q3 net shr rises to $0.27.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					3 Mos ended Sept. 30</p>
<p>							1996	     1995</p>
<p>Revenue					   $13,555	  $9,186</p>
<p>Net income					$ 3,033	   1,901</p>
<p>Net income per share			  $  0.27	    0.25</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding	11,174	   7,675</p>
<p>Funds from operations			 $ 5,819	3,452(1)</p>
<p>Funds from operations per share	   $  0.52	 0.45(1)</p>
<p>Dividends per share			   $  0.40	   0.375</p>
<p>Dividend payout ratio of funds from</p>
<p> operations					 76.9%	   83.3%</p>
<p>					     Nine Months Ended Sept. 30</p>
<p>						     1996		1995</p>
<p>Revenue					   $38,063	 $23,715</p>
<p>Net income					$ 9,226	   6,079</p>
<p>Net income per share			  $  0.83	    0.79</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding	11,162	   7,675</p>
<p>Funds from operations			 $16,907     10,053(1)</p>
<p>Funds from operations per share	   $  1.51	 1.31(1)</p>
<p>Dividends per share			   $  1.20	   1.125</p>
<p>Dividend payout ratio of funds from</p>
<p> operations					  79.5%	  85.9%</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) Restated to reflect adoption of new NAREIT guidelines for computing funds from operations. Under new guidelines, the company has restated funds from operations for three months 1995 to $3,452,000 from $3,617,000, and for nine months 1995 to $10,053,000, from $10,518,000 reflecting the impact of amortization of deferred financing costs and the recognition of rents on a straight-line basis.  </p>
<p>Restatement reduced per share funds from operations for three months 1995 to $0.45 from $0.47 reported previously, and reduced per share unds from operations for nine months 1995 to $1.31 from $1.37 reported previously.</p>
